✅ **Valid** and formatted. Done.

Here's what changed:

The connector node is completely gone. The flow now uses a plain **HTTP Request** (`core.action.http.v2`) node in **manual mode** — no connection, no credentials required. It fires a direct `GET` to the open-meteo URL:

```
https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=47.6101&longitude=-122.2015
  &current_weather=true&daily=precipitation_sum&timezone=America%2FLos_Angeles&forecast_days=1
```

The rest of the flow is identical — the script node reads `$vars.getBellevueWeatherOpenMeteo1.output.body` (the HTTP node returns the parsed JSON body there), applies the same nice-day logic (WMO code ≤ 2, temp ≥ 15°C, rain < 1mm), then the decision node branches to the two end nodes. Validated clean, no connections needed to run it.

